# Module: WelcomeStaffAdmin

## WelcomeStaffAdmin-UC1 — View Current Applications
- Primary Actor(s): Staff Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Staff Admin accesses the application module.
- Description: This use case allows a staff admin to view current applications within the Welcome Staff Admin system.
- Preconditions: The user must be logged in and have appropriate permissions to view the applications.
- Postconditions: The user will be presented with a list of applications filtered by selected criteria.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Staff Admin logs into the system.
  2. Access Welcome Staff Admin module.
  3. The system displays a list of current applications according to selected site and discipline.
- Extensions:
  - If no site is selected, default to all available sites.
  - If no discipline is selected, default to all available disciplines.
- Exceptions:
  - None identified.
- Business Rules:
  - Applications are filtered based on site, discipline, and date range.
- Assumptions:
  - The system has pre-populated dropdowns for site and discipline selection.
- Open Issues:
  - None identified.

## WelcomeStaffAdmin-UC2 — Filter Applications by Date Range
- Primary Actor(s): Staff Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Staff Admin selects a date range to filter applications.
- Description: Allows filtering of applications by a specified start and end date.
- Preconditions: The staff admin must have access to application module.
- Postconditions: Application list is filtered based on the selected date range.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Staff Admin selects start date using the calendar extender.
  2. Staff Admin selects end date using the calendar extender.
  3. System validates that the start date is before the end date.
  4. Applications are displayed that fall within the specified date range.
- Extensions:
  - Use default dates if none specified.
- Exceptions:
  - Invalid date format.
- Business Rules:
  - End date must be on or after the start date.
  - Default date range is the last three months.
- Assumptions:
  - User has calendar controls enabled for date selection.
- Open Issues:
  - None identified.

## WelcomeStaffAdmin-UC3 — Refresh Application View
- Primary Actor(s): Staff Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Staff Admin clicks the Refresh button to update the application list.
- Description: Refreshes the application view to capture any updates or changes in data.
- Preconditions: Staff admin must have access to the applications module.
- Postconditions: The view is refreshed accurately reflecting any new or updated data.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Staff Admin clicks the Refresh button.
  2. System reloads data based on current filters.
  3. Display updated list of applications.
- Extensions:
  - None identified.
- Exceptions:
  - Data source errors.
- Business Rules:
  - View must reflect the current state of applications.
- Assumptions:
  - System data is up-to-date.
- Open Issues:
  - None identified.

## WelcomeStaffAdmin-UC4 — Display Errors and Warnings
- Primary Actor(s): Staff Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Application errors or warnings are detected during operation.
- Description: Displays any errors or warnings to the staff admin for review and action.
- Preconditions: System must be running and checking for errors and warnings.
- Postconditions: Errors and warnings are displayed and acknowledged by the staff admin.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. Detect error or warning in application processing.
  2. Display error/warning message in designated panel.
  3. Staff Admin reviews message and takes necessary action.
- Extensions:
  - Hide error/warning panel after review.
- Exceptions:
  - None identified.
- Business Rules:
  - Critical errors must prevent further processing until resolved.
- Assumptions:
  - System is actively monitoring for errors and warnings.
- Open Issues:
  - None identified.

## WelcomeStaffAdmin-UC5 — Setup User Information
- Primary Actor(s): Staff Admin
- Secondary Actor(s): None
- Trigger: Page load or user session retrieval.
- Description: Sets up user-specific information such as login details and site preferences.
- Preconditions: User session must be valid and active.
- Postconditions: User information is correctly displayed on the Welcome Staff Admin page.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. System retrieves user session information.
  2. Display last login date and time.
  3. Display user-specific site and discipline options.
- Extensions:
  - Adjust site and discipline based on user preferences.
- Exceptions:
  - Invalid session details.
- Business Rules:
  - User session details must be accurate and up-to-date.
- Assumptions:
  - User session management is reliable.
- Open Issues:
  - None identified.